    "referrals": [
      "POL-RD-09(4) billing integrity: the SGD 3.20 'Bukit Merah Central westbound' ERP line is a phantom gantry charge — the platform's own proximity check puts the vehicle's nearest GPS fix 7,482 m from the gantry coordinates, roughly thirty times the 250 m crossing radius, with no bracketing gap — and it has been refunded in full as a standalone correction."
    ],
    "confidence": 0.9,
    "explanation": "To both parties: this was an upfront-quoted RydeX trip. The booking quote was SGD 22.00 and the final charge was SGD 25.20; the whole difference is the single SGD 3.20 ERP line for the 'Bukit Merah Central westbound' gantry. That line cannot stand, and the entire contested sum is returned. FULL_REFUND records that the filing party is entirely right on the SGD 3.20 contested.\n\nWhy the gantry line falls. The platform's own derived check against the GPS trace places the vehicle's nearest fix 7,482 m from the gantry coordinates — about thirty times the 250 m radius used to match a gantry to a trace — and reports no bracketing gaps and a false gap-bracketed closest approach, so the car does not cross it on any reading. The trace itself is clean and unimpaired for policy purposes: 169 fixes at a 10-second interval, 100% coverage, no gaps, a maximum gap of 0.0 seconds, no jump over 500 m and no sustained interval above 30 seconds, so POL-RD-07 has no purchase and this finding is read off a sound trace rather than inferred from a hole. Both accounts agree: the driver's own statement on file says he did not see or pass the gantry named on the receipt, and the rider's only chat message queries that same line. The SGD 3.20 is therefore a billing-integrity failure refunded in full under POL-RD-09(4), available whether or not a deviation exists. It is also exactly the amount by which the SGD 25.20 charged exceeds the SGD 22.00 quote with no properly chargeable pass-through line (the fare's on-optimal-route ERP total is SGD 0.00), which POL-RD-11(a) returns. These are the same SGD 3.20, counted once, not added together.\n\nThe route deviation, and why it moves no money. The trace measures 16.0 km against a 12.5 km optimal route — a 3.5 km excess, 28.0% of optimal — which clears both POL-RD-01 establishment limbs (over 20% and over 0.8 km). It is not a MATERIAL deviation (below 50% and below 8.0 km), so the POL-RD-06 driver_profile check is not engaged; in any event driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d is 0 against 610 completed trips in 90 days, so no repeat-deviation pattern exists and no FULL_REFUND uplift of charged_total and no POL-RD-06(c) conduct referral can attach. On an upfront-quoted trip POL-RD-11 fixes the distance and time charges at booking, so POL-RD-02 does not run and no distance-or-time refund is available on the excess: the loss on the detour falls on the driver, and the rider's remedies are confined to the pass-through and statutory lines. There is no unbilled distance to compensate either — 16.0 km was billed against 16.0 km traced — so no driver compensation is payable.\n\nThe rider's POL-RD-03 point (the traffic advisory is MISSING, weight 0.0, issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT, so it could not exonerate the deviation) is correct as far as it goes, but nothing turns on it: the driver has not asserted a closure or any other exculpation, no limb needs the clause to hold or fail for the money, and the deviation costs the rider nothing on an upfront fare. The absence is noted, no escalation flows from it.\n\nNo escalation trigger fires. The trip identifiers match across trip_record, gps_trace and fare_breakdown (all TRP-09114); the trace is unimpaired; pickup and dropoff timestamps are consistent; confidence rests on deciding artifacts at weight 1.0, above the 0.70 floor; the refund is far below the SGD 150.00 ceiling; and the only unmatched charge line is the ERP line refunded under POL-RD-09(4), which POL-RD-10(8) expressly excludes. The dispute is fully decidable on this record.\n\nOutcome: the disputed amount of SGD 3.20 is not collected; it is returned to the rider in full, and the SGD 3.20 phantom ERP line is referred as a billing-integrity finding under POL-RD-09(4)."
  },
  "discarded_claims": []
}
